  "title": "AlloyDB Read Pool Autoscaling Arrives",
  "summary": "AlloyDB now supports autoscaling for read pools, allowing you to dynamically adjust read replica capacity based on CPU utilization and predefined schedules. This enhances performance and cost efficiency for read-heavy workloads.",
  "details": "The AlloyDB API introduces new schemas (`AutoScalingConfig`, `CpuUtilization`, `Policy`, `Schedule`) to enable comprehensive autoscaling for read pools. You can now configure autoscaling via the `ReadPoolConfig.autoScalingConfig` property. This includes defining CPU utilization targets (`CpuUtilization.utilizationTarget`), setting maximum node counts (`Policy.maxNodeCount`), and scheduling scaling events using cron expressions (`Schedule.cronExpression`) with specific durations and minimum node counts. This feature allows for more efficient resource management and improved responsiveness to varying read loads.",
